# Environment variables
# .env is intentionally committed on this Lovable classic Vite stack — it holds
# only the PUBLIC Supabase URL + publishable (anon) key that Vite inlines into
# the client bundle at build time. Ignoring it breaks the published build with
# "Missing VITE_SUPABASE_URL or VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY". Never put
# service-role keys or real secrets in .env — those go in Project Settings → Secrets.
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env

